{
    "word": "piteous",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                "word": "piteous",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "571bb14b-1e55-4e5b-809e-181167fb452c",
                        "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more piteous"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4be947c4-d228-4154-b06b-d7ddd5e695dd",
                        "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most piteous"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ffdfb0ac-16c6-3864-bde3-4b76977c822d",
                        "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Provoking pity, compassion, or sympathy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "84c9da73-f204-4d19-ba6e-42e2260e2aaf",
                                "sense_id": "ffdfb0ac-16c6-3864-bde3-4b76977c822d",
                                "text": "[…] with his strong arms\nHe fastened on my neck, and bellowed out\nAs he’d burst heaven; threw him on my father;\nTold the most piteous tale of Lear and him\nThat ever ear receiv’d;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c26c516c-8897-4c7b-b9de-151e4ebdfde8",
                                "sense_id": "ffdfb0ac-16c6-3864-bde3-4b76977c822d",
                                "text": "1782, Frances Burney, Cecilia, London: T. Payne & Son and T. Cadell, Volume 2, Book 3, Chapter 4, p. 51,\n[…] my strength, madam, is almost all gone away, and when I do any hard work, it’s quite a piteous sight to see me, for I am all in a tremble after it, just as if I had an ague […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f822b89a-6561-48c1-9771-f5798a1afbe5",
                                "sense_id": "ffdfb0ac-16c6-3864-bde3-4b76977c822d",
                                "text": "In the deep, still darkness of midnight, I have been often aroused by the dead, heavy footsteps and the piteous cries of the chained gangs that passed our door."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dba7b58b-ac76-40c8-bca0-169171757477",
                                "sense_id": "ffdfb0ac-16c6-3864-bde3-4b76977c822d",
                                "text": "“[…] you go out to beg, first smearing yourself with mud and filth to make yourselves as piteous as you can.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "560e56c2-c922-48c3-97b9-0888dd32ca0b",
                                "sense_id": "ffdfb0ac-16c6-3864-bde3-4b76977c822d",
                                "text": "As fear chilled him to the bone, he loosed a final piteous groan."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3eb5b8c2-ac39-3f1b-b010-b407697fca85",
                        "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Showing devotion to God."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a32414e3-38ce-4467-b07b-f14dabfb2944",
                                "sense_id": "3eb5b8c2-ac39-3f1b-b010-b407697fca85",
                                "text": "For the Lord kan delyuere piteuouse men fro temptacioun, and kepe wickid men in to the dai of dom to be turmentid;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9f7cb6c7-58fa-3015-9516-9496af925638",
                        "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Showing compassion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2fc5ed6-735e-42ad-89fa-64ae46af0fb6",
                                "sense_id": "9f7cb6c7-58fa-3015-9516-9496af925638",
                                "text": "Thine eye begins to speak; set thy tongue there;\nOr in thy piteous heart plant thou thine ear;\nThat hearing how our plaints and prayers do pierce,\nPity may move thee ‘pardon’ to rehearse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "983b571c-9a32-4e22-a6e5-a4ed807cdfb4",
                                "sense_id": "9f7cb6c7-58fa-3015-9516-9496af925638",
                                "text": "The water Nymphs that in the bottome playd\nHeld up their pearled wrists and tooke her in,\nBearing her straite to aged Nereus hall\nWho piteous of her woes rea[r’]d her lanke head,\nAnd gave her to his daughters to imbathe\nIn nectar’d lavers strewd with asphodil,",
                                "translation": "Comus",
                                "english": "Comus"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae043f2e-7e54-4b1a-ba9b-44ebc659540a",
                                "sense_id": "9f7cb6c7-58fa-3015-9516-9496af925638",
                                "text": "With that the Goddess (piteous of his case,\nYet smiling at his ruful length of face)\nGives him a cov’ring,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "070f8a0c-b01e-4a27-8f1b-395c56c21e0d",
                                "sense_id": "9f7cb6c7-58fa-3015-9516-9496af925638",
                                "text": "Or have they soft piteous eyes beheld\nThe weary wanderer thro’ the desert rove?\nOr does th’ afflicted man thy heavenly bosom move?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6dcfb2b7-7ee1-39a1-8ea0-025ded32c03d",
                        "entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of little importance or value."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7922e7f8-cd01-4a91-914f-df540b27c6e6",
                                "sense_id": "6dcfb2b7-7ee1-39a1-8ea0-025ded32c03d",
                                "text": "[…] calling to minde with heed\nPart of our Sentence, that thy Seed shall bruise\nThe Serpents head; piteous amends, unless\nBe meant, whom I conjecture, our grand Foe\nSatan,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77102b03-11eb-4037-a0d2-149327389eb3",
                                "sense_id": "6dcfb2b7-7ee1-39a1-8ea0-025ded32c03d",
                                "text": "[…] my Business was now to try if I could not make Jackets out of the great Watch-Coats which I had by me, and with such other Materials as I had, so I set to Work a Taylering, or rather indeed a Botching, for I made most piteous Work of it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6700d9c4-219f-4c5d-bfb9-715f62bfeecb",
                        "source_entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "source_sense_description": "pitiful",
                        "target_lang_word": "žalostný",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f097968f-8700-4661-a055-37cafac2f495",
                        "source_entry_id": "82613015-6870-3401-9636-1bfa6f5f8abb",
                        "source_sense_description": "pitiful",
                        "target_lang_word": "pitoyable",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pitoyable",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                        "entry_id": "7727056f-47d0-3f43-b3d6-1e9a07babe32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est naturellement enclin à la pitié."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6352710b-66f0-46e0-9f84-3ecab6df0184",
                                                "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                                "text": "[…] je dis que tout prince doit désirer d’être tenu pour pitoyable et non pour cruel : cependant il doit prendre garde de ne point mal user de cette pitié."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a784bbde-2f8b-4809-84ec-29a2dd81058e",
                                                "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                                "text": "[…], Jacques examina ses malades, pitoyable devant toute cette misère, toute cette souffrance qu’il devait adoucir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04ae8a12-4aa3-4450-877c-0e103938f485",
                                                "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                                "text": "Chose difficile à croire et pourtant certaine, son époux fut affligé de cette mort, tant il avait l’âme pitoyable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "725d825f-548a-4fa6-b2c8-01c5a1432e82",
                                                "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                                "text": "Ces gens là, quelque pitoyables que nous nous montrions pour eux, nous garderont jusqu’au bout la même haine inexpiable ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc679e31-6c06-4a7d-90f5-787e42d183d1",
                                                "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                                "text": "Soyez pitoyables Et donnez du pain À de pauvres diables, Qui meurent de faim…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91b6c014-c9b0-4306-b845-e06ea0e25c64",
                                                "sense_id": "c03acaf1-424f-309f-9cee-bacfe7da26f2",
                                                "text": "Antoine et ma belle-sœur jouaient bien leur jeu ; ils se montraient, à mon égard, pitoyables, ils ne procédaient que par des allusions contristées. J'étais presque leur dupe, mais non pas entièrement !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2a2b277-ffc6-307d-a951-4c700b54fc5e",
                                        "entry_id": "7727056f-47d0-3f43-b3d6-1e9a07babe32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui excite la pitié."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Plus courant"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40cc66a4-f357-40be-acb9-fef7cb6e77c1",
                                                "sense_id": "e2a2b277-ffc6-307d-a951-4c700b54fc5e",
                                                "text": "Je ne sais pas de situation plus pitoyable que d’être bloqué par un brouillard humide sous le 66ᵉ degré de latitude nord; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c35cae9-7237-4a4e-8cf4-8fcf693b00fd",
                                                "sense_id": "e2a2b277-ffc6-307d-a951-4c700b54fc5e",
                                                "text": "Elle pleurait simplement, sans aucun sanglot, mais n'en paraissait que plus pitoyable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9263cce8-d45a-4791-8301-aaa11681198e",
                                                "sense_id": "e2a2b277-ffc6-307d-a951-4c700b54fc5e",
                                                "text": "Rien entre nous, que des souvenirs assez pitoyables, le tas lugubre des dèches quotidiennes, des privations et des désespérances."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c014ab07-b760-32d6-83cc-c0cbd06015ca",
                                        "entry_id": "7727056f-47d0-3f43-b3d6-1e9a07babe32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui inspire une pitié méprisante, qui est mauvais dans son genre, qui est digne de mépris."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "960b3f6a-d3ee-48d6-a75b-66cb8f872648",
                                                "sense_id": "c014ab07-b760-32d6-83cc-c0cbd06015ca",
                                                "text": "Oui, sans doute, il est pitoyable que des personnes aisées occupent indûment des lits dans les hôpitaux."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b909d7b5-56ee-431a-a3fb-97cd9f13d1b2",
                                                "sense_id": "c014ab07-b760-32d6-83cc-c0cbd06015ca",
                                                "text": "[…] : les prétendus beaux-esprits qui se trouvent parmi eux ne sont que de pitoyables bavards que le plus petit philosophe crotté; qui court les rues de Paris , mettrait à quia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
